governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different output changes, and each would need a different contract. Right now `todo list` prints only "[ ] title". It leaves out the ids, which `complete` needs, and the due dates. I need to know which changes are wanted before I can write a testable spec.)
governor asks: What should "easier to read" change? Right now `todo list` prints lines like "[ ] buy milk" with no id and no due date. Here's what I'd suggest: each line shows the id, a checkbox, the title and the due date if there is one, with the columns lined up. For example:
  #1  [ ] buy milk  (due 2026-11-01)
  #2  [x] walk dog
  #3  [ ] pay rent  (due 2026-10-31)
Should I go with that? Or do you also want any of these: sort by due date, put completed items last, hide completed items by default, add a summary line (e.g. "2 open, 1 done"), or use colours? Should the messages from add, complete and errors change too, or only the list?

